allowed `message`/`category` fields.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","E1"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"with only `stage`, `category`, `status_code`, `provider_code`, `retry_after_ms`, and `message`\"","\"uses entry eight as `(stage=diagnostic, category=truncated, dropped=N)`\""],"finding":"The diagnostic entry schema lists exactly six fields (stage, category, status_code, provider_code, retry_after_ms, message), but the overflow sentinel is specified as `(stage=diagnostic, category=truncated, dropped=N)` — introducing a `dropped` field that is not in the declared schema. The executor cannot tell whether the sentinel is a schema exception or whether `dropped=N` should be carried in `message`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffcb92aad9e12d7e9","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — diagnostics bullet","norm_id":"n62b09ae973e57829","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Nine diagnostic entries trigger the overflow sentinel and the executor must serialize entry eight canonically"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that the sentinel carries the drop count in `message` (e.g. message=\"dropped=N\") so it fits the six-field schema, or explicitly declare `dropped` as a seventh optional integer field and define its sorted-key position.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the complete lowercase member set for each of `disposition`, `failure_scope`, `replay_safety`, and `delay_source` in the plan (or in ADR 0100) so canonical serialization is fully determined.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"`disposition`, `failure_scope`, `replay_safety`, and `delay_source` serialize as fixed lowercase enum strings.\"","No enumeration of the concrete members for disposition/failure_scope/delay_source appears anywhere in the plan."],"finding":"The `disposition`, `failure_scope`, and `delay_source` enums are said to 'serialize as fixed lowercase enum strings' but their member sets are never enumerated. Only some values appear incidentally (commit_unknown for replay_safety). The executor must invent the complete member list, which the canonical-serialization contract depends on.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7aed5ad6c12f9ff7","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — contract bullet 2","norm_id":"nbad53adae05692a5","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author of operation_outcome.py must choose the disposition members (e.g. success/failed/commit_unknown) and delay_source members (e.g. jitter/provider)"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that operation_outcome.py serializes through the existing rebar._store.canonical.canonical_str/canonical_bytes seam (ascii_only=False) rather than a new inline json.dumps, or justify why a separate canonical serializer is required.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_store/canonical.py:57-66 canonical_str(doc, ascii_only=False) = json.dumps(ensure_ascii=False, separators=(',',':'), sort_keys=True) — identical to the plan's stated byte form","canonical.py docstring: 'the one true canonical-JSON/hash home' for 'sorted-key compact JSON' sites that 'had each reimplemented it inline' — an explicit warning against a new copy","Already reused in-reconciler: mutation.py:14, inbound_translate.py:244, dispatch_one.py:273, conflict_resolver.py:21 (>=3 call-sites)","The plan's Grounding section names ADR 0084 and ADR 0041 but omits any mention of the canonical serializer seam"],"finding":"The plan mandates canonical serialization (UTF-8 JSON, sorted keys, compact separators, no ASCII escaping) in a new operation_outcome.py but never references